## JavaScript API (`window.Cyrena.Runtime`)

### Runtime Lifecycle Functions

| Function | Signature | Purpose |
|----------|-----------|---------|
| `initializeRuntime` | `(elementId: string, dotNetRef: DotNetObjectReference) => void` | Binds a DOM element to a .NET object reference |
| `updateRuntime` | `(elementId: string, data: object) => void` | Sends data to .NET via `invokeMethodAsync('OnRuntimeUpdated', data)` |
| `disposeRuntime` | `(elementId: string) => void` | Cleans up the instance and disposes the .NET reference |

### Clipboard Paste Handler Functions

| Function | Signature | Purpose |
|----------|-----------|---------|
| `registerChatPasteHandler` | `(textarea: HTMLElement, dotNetHelper: DotNetObjectReference) => void` | Attaches a `paste` event listener to a textarea that intercepts pasted images (e.g. screenshots) and forwards them to .NET |
| `unregisterChatPasteHandler` | `(textarea: HTMLElement) => void` | Removes the `paste` event listener from a textarea and cleans up the internal handler map |

### `registerChatPasteHandler` Behavior

- Listens for `paste` events on the provided textarea element.
- Scans `e.clipboardData.items` for image MIME types (`image/*`).
- On detecting an image:
  - Calls `e.preventDefault()` to stop default paste behavior.
  - Reads the image blob via `FileReader.readAsDataURL()`.
  - Invokes `dotNetHelper.invokeMethodAsync('OnImagePasted', base64DataUrl, mimeType)`.
- Uses an internal `Map<textarea, handler>` to prevent duplicate registration.
- Logs warnings if a handler is already registered for the same textarea.

### `unregisterChatPasteHandler` Behavior

- Looks up the stored handler for the textarea in the internal `pasteHandlers` Map.
- Calls `textarea.removeEventListener('paste', handler)`.
- Deletes the entry from the Map.
- Logs a warning if no handler was registered.

### C# Invocation Examples

```csharp
// Register paste handler on a textarea ElementReference
await _js.InvokeVoidAsync("Cyrena.Runtime.registerChatPasteHandler", _area, _dotNetRef);

// Unregister on dispose
_ = _js.InvokeVoidAsync("Cyrena.Runtime.unregisterChatPasteHandler", _area);
```

### .NET Callback Contract

The .NET component must expose a `[JSInvokable]` method named `OnImagePasted`:

```csharp
[JSInvokable]
public void OnImagePasted(string base64DataUrl, string mimeType)
{
    // base64DataUrl: "data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgo..."
    // mimeType:      "image/png", "image/jpeg", etc.
}
```

### Blazor Component Usage Pattern

```csharp
public partial class Chat : IDisposable
{
    [Inject] private IJSRuntime _js { get; set; } = default!;
    private DotNetObjectReference<Chat>? _dotNetRef;
    private ElementReference _area; // the textarea

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (!firstRender) return;
        _dotNetRef = DotNetObjectReference.Create(this);
        await _js.InvokeVoidAsync("Cyrena.Runtime.registerChatPasteHandler", _area, _dotNetRef);
    }

    [JSInvokable]
    public void OnImagePasted(string base64DataUrl, string mimeType)
    {
        var extension = mimeType switch
        {
            "image/png" => "png",
            "image/jpeg" => "jpg",
            "image/gif" => "gif",
            "image/webp" => "webp",
            _ => "png"
        };

        var base64Data = base64DataUrl.Contains(',')
            ? base64DataUrl.Split(',')[1]
            : base64DataUrl;

        var bytes = Convert.FromBase64String(base64Data);
        var imageContent = new ImageContent(bytes, mimeType);
        var additionalContent = new AdditionalMessageContent($"pasted-image.{extension}", imageContent);
        _items.Add(additionalContent);
        InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        if (_dotNetRef is not null)
        {
            _ = _js.InvokeVoidAsync("Cyrena.Runtime.unregisterChatPasteHandler", _area);
            _dotNetRef.Dispose();
        }
    }
}
```

### Supported Image MIME Types

The paste handler recognizes any clipboard item where `item.type.indexOf('image') === 0`. Common types:
- `image/png`
- `image/jpeg`
- `image/gif`
- `image/webp`
- `image/bmp`

### Architecture Notes

- All functions live inside an IIFE with `'use strict'`.
- Two internal `Map` instances: `instances` (for runtime lifecycle) and `pasteHandlers` (for clipboard handlers).
- No global pollution except `window.Cyrena.Runtime`.
- Error handling: logs to `console.error`/`console.warn` but does not throw for missing elements or unregistered handlers.
- The `dotNetHelper` reference passed to `registerChatPasteHandler` is **not** disposed by the JS — the .NET side must call `unregisterChatPasteHandler` and then `Dispose()` on the `DotNetObjectReference`.
